-- The Isle of Four Winds. Generated by `codex fwi`; do not hand-edit.
--
-- A trinket you turn. 14 town squares reach Gardenia Commons with it,
-- and turning it on the island takes you back to the room you left --
-- the map database keeps that in `mapdb_fwi_return_room`, which is what
-- a destination of kind `origin` is for.
--
-- Every one of those roads is a `;e` script edge, so the extractor
-- dropped all of them and the island had no published way in at all.
--
-- The gate is the cost function, as usual:
--
--   ;e (!UserVars.mapdb_fwi_trinket.nil? and
--       !UserVars.mapdb_fwi_trinket.empty?) ? 15.0 : nil
--
-- Fifteen seconds if you have one, impassable if you do not.

-- Two gates. The trinket has no fixed name -- players own different
-- ones -- so it is named by a setting rather than written down here,
-- and a character who has not named theirs is not offered the road.

   'Turn the Four Winds trinket, from a town square to the island.');
  VALUES ('fwi:trinket:out', 'fixed', 3201029, 0,
    'turn my #{setting:travel/fwi_trinket}', 'You get the feeling', 15000);

-- The way back. `origin` rather than a room, because the trinket
-- returns you to where you came from and no row can name that in
-- advance -- which is exactly the kind the schema has for it.
--
-- The island is named by its `location` facets rather than by listing
-- thirteen hundred uids. The private homes file under their own names
-- ("Arborsong, inside the island town of Mist Harbor") and the
-- trinket works there too.
   'Turn the Four Winds trinket again, back to where you left.');
  VALUES ('fwi:trinket:home', 'origin', 0, 0,
    'turn my #{setting:travel/fwi_trinket}', 'You get the feeling', 15000);
